From: marcus040473 <marcus040473@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:36:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Gridfinity bins and trays as large as the chosen printer's
 bed (Discussion #1917)

A bin's units across and deep and a tray's width and length were held to
6 units, 252 mm. The fields now offer as much as the bed of the printer
chosen in the workspace settings takes: on a 330 x 320 mm bed a bin takes
7 units (293.5 mm) and a tray 330 mm. Without a printer they stay at 6
units and 252 mm. A drag, a file or the MCP is kept to 504 mm, so a bin
made for a large bed keeps its size. Baseplates keep their 6 units, or
12 on a large plate, and are split for a smaller bed as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
